---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const title = "Cookies";
const description =
  "Every cookie and browser-storage key ListBulkly uses, and the fact that there are no advertising or analytics cookies.";
---

<LegalLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <p>
    <strong>Draft.</strong> This is the complete list for this build. It stays a
    draft until the legal entity is added; the contact address below is real.
  </p>

  <h2>No advertising or analytics cookies</h2>
  <p>
    ListBulkly sets no advertising cookies, no analytics cookies and no tracking
    pixels. There is no third-party tag manager, no session recording and no
    cross-site profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase session cookie</strong> — set only after sign-in is enabled and
      you sign in. It keeps you signed in and is removed when the session ends or you
      sign out. Before authentication is switched on, this cookie does not exist.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Browser storage that is not a cookie</h2>
  <p>
    The workspace needs local storage to work at all. It is stored for this site's
    origin only and is not sent to our server automatically.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>IndexedDB</strong> — the library: artwork, mockups, print areas, renders, listing drafts, export history, activity, and the API keys you paste in Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>localStorage</strong> — small preferences such as whether the sidebar is collapsed, the selected Printify shop, and the companion-extension handshake marker.</li>
    <li><strong>sessionStorage</strong> — short-lived UI state, such as which chat turn is open.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Clearing it</h2>
  <p>
    Clearing this site's data in your browser removes the library and every stored
    preference. The Settings page also has a "Clear keys from this browser" action.
    Export anything you need first: the Export Center produces a ZIP.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about cookies: <a href="mailto:listbulkly@gmail.com">listbulkly@gmail.com</a>.
    See also <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a> and the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
